# {{.Name}}

A Caja **web-app** project — `main.caja` imports the `browser` module and
compiles to a WebAssembly binary that runs entirely client-side. The page
itself is built as a View tree (`mount()`, from `@caja/dom`, walks it into
live DOM nodes) rather than a hand-written HTML string — see `main.caja` for
the pattern, and https://www.cajalang.com for more.

Four packages, all imported by `main.caja`: `@caja/siriguela` is the theme
(the components that carry the look), `@caja/ui` is the structural layer it
is built on (the View tree, and the JavaScript event handlers), `@caja/js`
builds that JavaScript, and `@caja/dom` is the renderer — which also owns
the `onClick` family that takes a **Caja** function, since attaching one
needs the Caja runtime this wasm build ships. siriguela does not re-export
ui, so both are imported directly.

`package.json` declares all three, and `caja init` runs your package
manager's install for you. **None of them is published to npm yet**, though,
so that install currently fails with a warning — until they are, link them
manually into a `node_modules/` at or above this folder:

```
node_modules/@caja/siriguela   ->  the theme
node_modules/@caja/ui          ->  the structural layer
node_modules/@caja/dom         ->  the renderer (mount/sync)
node_modules/@caja/js          ->  the JavaScript builder @caja/ui uses
```

## Development

```
caja serve
```

Builds the project to wasm and serves it (with its HTML/JS harness) over
HTTP for local development.

## Building

```
caja build
```

Compiles `main.caja` to `{{.Name}}.wasm`, and writes `wasm_exec.js`,
`{{.Name}}.html`, and `index.html` alongside it.

## Deploying

The build output directory is a self-contained static bundle
(`{{.Name}}.wasm`, `wasm_exec.js`, `index.html`) — point any static file host
(Netlify, GitHub Pages, S3 + CloudFront, nginx, ...) at it and visitors
navigating to your domain will receive `index.html`, which loads and runs
the wasm binary in their browser.
